      "biography": {
        "value": "<h2>Description</h2><p>Large quadrupedal mammal that forms herds around a matriarch. This gentle giant can be found all around the plains. Gentle by nature, the Garula only attacks when provoked.</p><h2>Defense</h2><p>AC 22, touch 9, flat-footed 22 (+13 natural, -1 size)</p><p>hp 147 [196] (14d8+84)</p><p>Fort +16; Ref +9; Will +5</p><p>Resist Ice 15, Earth 10</p><h2>Offense</h2><p>Speed 40 ft.</p><p>Melee gore +20 (2d4+10), slam +20 (1d6+10), 2 stomps +18 (2d4+5)</p><p>Space 10 ft.; Reach 5 ft.</p><p>Special Attacks Trample (1d6+15, DC 22)</p><h2>Statistics</h2><p>Str 30, Dex 10, Con 20, Int 2, Wis 13, Cha 6</p><p>Base Atk +10; CMB +21 (+23 bull rush); CMD 31 (33 vs. bull rush, 35 vs. trip)</p><p>Feats Great Fortitude, Improved Bull Rush, Multiattack, Toughness, Weapon Focus (slam), Weapon Focus (stomp), Weapon Focus (gore)</p><p>Skills Climb +12, Perception +15</p>"
